187,2555,92,220,16,488,259,24984,220,18,83,24984,220,16,481,259,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,60,48101,304,264,11031,315,279,1352,400,87,488,379,488,17988,284,294,2418,220,11252,279,11457,6716,4930,66,11991,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe line parameterized by\n\\[\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\]lies in a plane of the form $x + y + cz = d.$  Enter the ordered pair $(c,d).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"85b1c0e331e0ed798c0aaa2afa1023706b9842ceaf3f9ed294ff88558bb5b7c1"},"seconds":25.462115049362183,"seed":15994890039637181,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to find the values of \\(c\\) and \\(d\\) for the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\) such that the line parameterized by \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\) lies in this plane.\n\nFirst, we express the coordinates of the line in terms of the parameter \\(t\\):\n\\[\nx = 1 + t, \\quad y = 3t, \\quad z = 1 - t.\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute these expressions into the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\):\n\\[\n(1 + t) + (3t) + c(1 - t) = d.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side:\n\\[\n1 + t + 3t + c(1 - t) = d,\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + 4t + c - ct = d,\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + c + t(4 - c) = d.\n\\]\n\nFor the line to lie in the plane, the equation must hold for all values of \\(t\\). This means the coefficients of \\(t\\) on the left-hand side must equal the coefficients of \\(t\\) on the right-hand side. Since \\(d\\) is a constant and does not depend on \\(t\\), the coefficient of \\(t\\) on the left-hand side must be zero:\n\\[\n4 - c = 0.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(c\\):\n\\[\nc = 4.\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(c = 4\\) back into the equation:\n\\[\n1 + 4 + t(4 - 4) = d,\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + 4 = d,\n\\]\n\\[\nd = 5.\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(4, 5)}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(4, 5)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve this problem, we need to find the values of \\(c\\) and \\(d\\) for the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\) such that the line parameterized by \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\) lies in this plane.\n\nFirst, we express the coordinates of the line in terms of the parameter \\(t\\):\n\\[\nx = 1 + t, \\quad y = 3t, \\quad z = 1 - t.\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute these expressions into the plane equation \\(x + y + cz = d\\):\n\\[\n(1 + t) + (3t) + c(1 - t) = d.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side:\n\\[\n1 + t + 3t + c(1 - t) = d,\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + 4t + c - ct = d,\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + c + t(4 - c) = d.\n\\]\n\nFor the line to lie in the plane, the equation must hold for all values of \\(t\\). This means the coefficients of \\(t\\) on the left-hand side must equal the coefficients of \\(t\\) on the right-hand side. Since \\(d\\) is a constant and does not depend on \\(t\\), the coefficient of \\(t\\) on the left-hand side must be zero:\n\\[\n4 - c = 0.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(c\\):\n\\[\nc = 4.\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(c = 4\\) back into the equation:\n\\[\n1 + 4 + t(4 - 4) = d,\n\\]\n\\[\n1 + 4 = d,\n\\]\n\\[\nd = 5.\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(4, 5)}.\n\\]","id":"precalculus:264"}
